{
  "Description": "feature.fillet on edges between cylinders and planes at oblique angles. Bodies: tiltedCylinders - a vertical cylinder (r 25, z 0..70) united with a tilted cylinder (r 20, axis from (20,10,5) to (20,-12,75)), like RoundEdges5: two concave intersection curves between the mantles, each ending at a cap (dead ends at faces oblique to the edge). tee - a vertical pipe (r 15) crossed by a horizontal one (r 10): two closed concave saddle curves. obliqueTee - the same with the cross pipe tilted (z 22..38). uprightBoss / tiltedBoss - a cylinder (r 12) standing on a plate 80x60x10, upright or tilted (axis (35,30,5)-(45,30,40)): the concave foot curve (circle resp. ellipse) and the convex rim at the top cap. uprightHoled / tiltedHoled - a block 60x60x20 drilled through by a cylinder (r 8), upright or tilted (axis (25,30,-10)-(35,30,30)): two convex rims. The upright variants have closed forms and anchor the tilted ones. Fillets: tiltedCylindersMid / Big (r 4 / 8, the two concave mantle curves), teeSaddles and obliqueTeeSaddles (r 3, the saddle curves), uprightBossFoot / tiltedBossFoot (r 3, the foot), uprightBossRim / tiltedBossRim (r 2, the top rim), uprightHoleRims / tiltedHoleRims (r 2, both rims).",
  "Expected": "A(r) = r^2 (1 - pi/4), M(r) = r^3 (5/6 - pi/4) (see FilletSingleEdges); by Pappus a fillet along a circle of radius R adds or removes 2 pi (R A +- M). uprightBoss = 48000 + 4320 pi = 61571.680264. uprightBossFoot: concave, the centroid lies outside the pin: 61571.680264 + 2 pi (12 A(3) + M(3)) = 61725.437649, one torus. uprightBossRim: convex, centroid inside: 61571.680264 - 2 pi (12 A(2) - M(2)) = 61509.367359, one torus. uprightHoleRims: convex, centroid outside the hole: 72000 - 1280 pi - 2 * 2 pi (8 A(2) + M(2)) = 67887.645916, two tori. The tilted and crossing variants have no closed form; expected: closed and consistent, the original faces plus one SweptCircleSurface or torus per rounded edge, no planes or extrusions beyond those of the body.",
  "CaseStatus": "Ok",
  "Status": "PASSES (2026-10-10). All ten fillets are closed and consistent and add exactly one SweptCircleSurface or torus per rounded edge. Exact against the closed forms: uprightBossFoot, uprightBossRim, uprightHoleRims and tiltedBossRim (the cap is perpendicular to the pin, so its rim is a torus: -2 pi (12 A(2) - M(2)) = -62.312905). The others agree with an independent numerical integration of the ideal rolling ball fillet (cross sections in the normal planes of the spine, validated against uprightBossFoot to 1e-4): tiltedBossFoot +170.910 (ideal 170.91), tiltedHoleRims -98.939 (98.94), teeSaddles +121.449 (121.41), obliqueTeeSaddles +130.549 (130.56), tiltedCylindersMid +68.266 (68.24) and Big +206.827 (206.67), the latter two with the fillet cut flat at the planes of the caps. The end edges of the tiltedCylinders fillets (transversal intersections with the caps) are up to 4.7e-6 off the fillet surface. Slow: teeSaddles about 29 s, obliqueTeeSaddles 15 s (Repeat is 1 for that reason).",
  "History": "2026-10-07: written after the dead end and tangential intersection fixes for RoundEdges5 (377c84d5, fbdad961): fillets and chamfers on cylinders which meet each other or planes at oblique angles. 2026-10-07: BlendEdges.createExtensionTwoEdges decides tangential connections from the 3d directions (TurnAngle): the 2d directions of the ProjectedCurves on the common face made a tangential connection look like a corner of 0.1 degree, and both end faces were extruded (obliqueTeeSaddles). 2026-10-10: fixed by PipeContactCurve (a8a156d1, 78d55591: exact curves of contact instead of tangential intersections, exact 2d curves also on reversed faces) and fixes in BooleanOperation; tiltedCylinders* no longer throw in ConnectOpenEdges. The former verified baselines of teeSaddles (+130.71) and obliqueTeeSaddles (4 of 8 fillets) were wrong.",
